<h1>Member Management for Teams & Clubs</h1>

<p class="lead">Member management software that keeps your roster, teams, and roles in one searchable place — so the knowledge isn't locked in one volunteer's spreadsheet.</p>

<img src="/images/ss-directory.png" srcset="/images/ss-directory.webp 826w, /images/ss-directory.png 826w" type="image/webp" alt="GatherPack member directory screenshot showing searchable roster with contact info, roles, and dietary restrictions" width="826" height="826" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;max-width:560px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;" class="rounded border">

<section id="overview" class="card" aria-labelledby="overview-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="overview-heading">A single source of truth for who's who</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>GatherPack gives every person one record: contact info, relationships, dietary restrictions, shirt sizes, history, and whatever else your organization tracks. Members edit their own information, so leaders aren't stuck updating rows for everyone. This is the foundation — teams, events, announcements, and finance all hang off the roster.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">Built from the lesson that first sparked GatherPack: a <a href="https://westside-robotics.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FIRST Robotics team</a> couldn't keep attendance and fundraising details straight because they lived in scattered sheets and sticky notes. The fix was a shared directory everyone could actually find. <a href="/about/">How we got here →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

