<section id="who-uses" class="card" aria-labelledby="who-uses-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="who-uses-heading">Who uses this</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>Member management is where most groups start because it immediately replaces the “only one person knows” problem. A <a href="/use-cases/nonprofits/">nonprofit</a> uses it to keep volunteers and coordinators straight; a <a href="/use-cases/churches/">church</a> uses it for families and small groups; <a href="/use-cases/first-robotics/">FIRST teams</a> use it for students, parents, and mentors across build and competition season.</p>
    <p>From there it connects: roster → <a href="/features/events/">events &amp; check-in</a> → <a href="/features/communication/">announcements</a> scoped to teams → <a href="/features/finance/">finance</a> tied to people. Same person, same record, no double entry.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">Compare sibling pillars: <a href="/features/events/">Event Management</a> · <a href="/features/finance/">Finance</a> · <a href="/features/communication/">Communication</a> · <a href="/features/automation/">Automation &amp; Reports</a></p>
